        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(media-understanding): apply imageMaxDimensionPx resize to image description input (#101923)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #101923. The image description pre-processing pipeline (`prepareImageDescriptionInput`) passes images through at original dimensions without applying `agents.defaults.imageMaxDimensionPx`. Phone-camera photos (typically 4000×8000) exceed provider limits and fail with:\n\n```\nImage dimensions exceed the 25,000,000 pixel input limit: 4536x8064\n```\n\nThis affects `openclaw infer image describe --model ...`, `describeImageFileWithModel`, and `describePreparedImageWithModel`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a `resizeToJpeg` step after `normalizeImageDescriptionInput` when `imageMaxDimensionPx` is configured, reusing the same image-ops resize ladder already used by the tool image output sanitizer.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — resizeToJpeg with maxSide=2000\n\nGenerates a 3000×3000 BMP (27MB), passes through the exact `resizeToJpeg` function used in `prepareImageDescriptionInput`, and verifies the result respects the 2000px limit:\n\n```\n=== Before resize ===\nDimensions: 3000x3000 | bytes: 27000054\n\n=== After resizeToJpeg(maxSide=2000) ===\nDimensions: 2000x2000 | bytes: 69717\nWithin 2000px limit: true\n\n✅ imageMaxDimensionPx enforcement works\n```\n\nRun with: `node --import tsx/esm -e \"import { resizeToJpeg, getImageMetadata } from './src/media/image-ops.ts'; ...\"`\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/media-understanding/runtime.ts` | +14: `resizeToJpeg` with `maxSide` from `imageMaxDimensionPx` when configured in `prepareImageDescriptionInput` |\n",
        "branch": "fix/media-resize-ladder-bypass",
